h264_mmal on Haiku: the VideoCore's H.264 decoder through MMAL

FFmpeg's MMAL decoders (libavcodec/mmaldec.c) on the Raspberry Pi 4 under
Haiku: Broadcom's libmmal/libvchiq/VCOS (raspberrypi_userland, BSD-3) over the
vchiq driver's /dev/vchiq. Haiku's media kit plugin picks h264_mmal for H.264
when it opens and falls back to h264 otherwise (haiku-rpi
docs/design/vchiq.md, step 3).

  configure    mmal found without bcm_host (raspberrypi_userland does not
               build it; the decoder only calls bcm_host_init()): libvchiq_arm
               and libvcos instead, as raspberrypi_userland's mmal.pc lists
  mmaldec.c    no bcm_host on Haiku; h264_mmal takes its packets through
               h264_mp4toannexb and sends the parameter sets as that filter
               outputs them (Annex-B, also for an "avcC" record) instead of
               avctx->extradata; a log line when the decoder is set up and one
               with the frame and packet counts when it is closed; the comma
               missing after caps_internal in FFMMAL_DEC (6.1 does not compile
               it); extra_buffers 2 instead of 10 (the VideoCore's memory, 76 MB
               on the Pi 4, holds no more: the decoder fails with ENOSPC and
               outputs empty frames); after an error event, or 2 s without a
               frame it owed, receive_frame() returns AVERROR_EXTERNAL from then
               on (the caller falls back to the software decoder) instead of
               logging every packet's error; a single 100 ms wait without a
               frame is no error; draining sends the end-of-stream buffer
               (since FFmpeg 5 the end comes as AVERROR_EOF from
               ff_decode_get_packet(), not as the empty packet mmaldec waited
               for, so the frames the decoder still held were lost) and waits
               for the decoder's last frames instead of returning EAGAIN; the
               decoder is kept supplied with 8 packets (receive_frame() asks
               for more before it returns a frame): a caller that sends a
               packet only when no frame is ready - Haiku's media plugin - let
               it run dry, and its next frame then came 70-90 ms late at 1080p

LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the files it changes.

